U5NGVkYmJmOTRmZmM3NTE1MTBmNzRhZmZkZmZlMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/decentraland/sites/commit/0d76b8a9470834ee52371fd750b4aa8e65ffb486","sha":"0d76b8a9470834ee52371fd750b4aa8e65ffb486","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/commits/0d76b8a9470834ee52371fd750b4aa8e65ffb486"}],"sha":"89b73ace7e94edbbf94ffc751510f74affdffe28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/commits/89b73ace7e94edbbf94ffc751510f74affdffe28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1120791?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LautaroPetaccio","id":1120791,"login":"LautaroPetaccio","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjA3OTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/commits/0d76b8a9470834ee52371fd750b4aa8e65ffb486/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:35:53Z","email":"1120791+LautaroPetaccio@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Lautaro Petaccio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:35:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: publish a release to zone instead of staging it (#874)\n\n* feat: publish a release to zone and today instead of staging it\n\nCutting a release uploaded the bytes under the tag and touched no KV record, so\nnothing served it until someone remembered to dispatch a promotion. It could\nnot have done more as written: the job declared no `environment:`, GitHub\ntherefore issued no environment claim, and the broker refuses `today` without\none. The empty list made that explicit rather than a failure.\n\nDeclaring `environment: today` supplies the claim, and one job covers both\ntargets — `zone` requires no claim at all, `today` requires one naming itself.\nVerified against the broker''s own publication policy with the token shape this\njob will actually carry: zone accepted, today accepted, org refused with\n`EnvironmentApprovalRequiredError`.\n\n`org` stays out deliberately. The broker would take it — the version is a tag,\nso the release requirement is satisfied — but production is promoted by hand,\nnaming the version, from the `promote` job.\n\nThe consequence worth stating: GitHub evaluates `environment:` BEFORE the job\nstarts, so once `today` has required reviewers, publishing a release waits for\none instead of deploying. That is the gate working rather than a regression,\nbut it changes what cutting a release feels like. Until those rules exist it\ndeploys immediately, with no approval — which is the argument for setting them.\n\nRenamed from `stage-release`, which described what it no longer does. Nothing\nreferenced the id: master''s ruleset declares no required status checks, only\ndeletion, non-fast-forward, pull-request and signature rules.\n\n* fix: keep prereleases out of the release rollout\n\n`release: published` fires for prereleases as well, so without a guard an RC\nwould publish to zone and today like any other release. No prerelease appears\nin the last 30 releases, so this costs nothing today and prevents a surprise\nthe first time someone cuts one.\n\n* fix: publish a release to zone only, without declaring an environment\n\n`today` admits protected branches only (`protected_branches: true`,\n`custom_branch_policies: false`), and a `release: published` run executes on\n`refs/tags/<tag>`. GitHub evaluates the declared environment''s deployment\npolicy before the job starts, so `environment: today` would stop this job\nbefore it uploaded anything -- leaving `promote` to `org` with no bytes to\npromote, which is worse than the staging it replaces.\n\n`zone` needs no environment claim, so a release now serves there directly\nrather than sitting in S3 until someone dispatches a promotion. `today` and\n`org` stay manual promotions from `promote`, which runs on master and does\nsatisfy the policy.\n\nAdmitting release tags to `today` would need it switched to \"Selected branches\nand tags\" with `master` re-added, and a tag ruleset to go with it: none exists,\nso tag creation would otherwise become deploy access to an environment on an\nunmerged commit.","tree":{"sha":"f2a72acb9c7bcb792e190ab7e2d07e8a369e2489","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/git/trees/f2a72acb9c7bcb792e190ab7e2d07e8a369e2489"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/git/commits/0d76b8a9470834ee52371fd750b4aa8e65ffb486","verification":{"payload":"tree f2a72acb9c7bcb792e190ab7e2d07e8a369e2489\nparent 5ad83d1f3871f31feafc43806be1c33d47931fcc\nauthor Lautaro Petaccio <1120791+LautaroPetaccio@users.noreply.github.com> 1790775353 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790775353 -0300\n\nfeat: publish a release to zone instead of staging it (#874)\n\n* feat: publish a release to zone and today instead of staging it\n\nCutting a release uploaded the bytes under the tag and touched no KV record, so\nnothing served it until someone remembered to dispatch a promotion. It could\nnot have done more as written: the job declared no `environment:`, GitHub\ntherefore issued no environment claim, and the broker refuses `today` without\none. The empty list made that explicit rather than a failure.\n\nDeclaring `environment: today` supplies the claim, and one job covers both\ntargets — `zone` requires no claim at all, `today` requires one naming itself.\nVerified against the broker''s own publication policy with the token shape this\njob will actually carry: zone accepted, today accepted, org refused with\n`EnvironmentApprovalRequiredError`.\n\n`org` stays out deliberately. The broker would take it — the version is a tag,\nso the release requirement is satisfied — but production is promoted by hand,\nnaming the version, from the `promote` job.\n\nThe consequence worth stating: GitHub evaluates `environment:` BEFORE the job\nstarts, so once `today` has required reviewers, publishing a release waits for\none instead of deploying. That is the gate working rather than a regression,\nbut it changes what cutting a release feels like. Until those rules exist it\ndeploys immediately, with no approval — which is the argument for setting them.\n\nRenamed from `stage-release`, which described what it no longer does. Nothing\nreferenced the id: master''s ruleset declares no required status checks, only\ndeletion, non-fast-forward, pull-request and signature rules.\n\n* fix: keep prereleases out of the release rollout\n\n`release: published` fires for prereleases as well, so without a guard an RC\nwould publish to zone and today like any other release. No prerelease appears\nin the last 30 releases, so this costs nothing today and prevents a surprise\nthe first time someone cuts one.\n\n* fix: publish a release to zone only, without declaring an environment\n\n`today` admits protected branches only (`protected_branches: true`,\n`custom_branch_policies: false`), and a `release: published` run executes on\n`refs/tags/<tag>`. GitHub evaluates the declared environment''s deployment\npolicy before the job starts, so `environment: today` would stop this job\nbefore it uploaded anything -- leaving `promote` to `org` with no bytes to\npromote, which is worse than the staging it replaces.\n\n`zone` needs no environment claim, so a release now serves there directly\nrather than sitting in S3 until someone dispatches a promotion. `today` and\n`org` stay manual promotions from `promote`, which runs on master and does\nsatisfy the policy.\n\nAdmitting release tags to `today` would need it switched to \"Selected branches\nand tags\" with `master` re-added, and a tag ruleset to go with it: none exists,\nso tag creation would otherwise become deploy access to an environment on an\nunmerged commit.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvRA5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACoQQAIWCyQ9iEfulmspiq2UV/kh9\nF/XaxRQOiYK5UDCTSuGaW0nEmz3chrgCjBsEh51mQYfitRcDkF99uqAzF2oH3LCA\nEiariT6gszPVoSmihN0uPmm7j2FuupGs8AOaE+zyfb/AuCXs+m9NdsZTAX0ewQeD\n1cmnhW7MHsj0wzqv8fMVexcsOd3IDUXLojdrcl483mLGtZHlyGCXNdF2iWwmdSmf\nuEcrUcfum73bAm0jt6niBkG0F4tOg6z+IsGTnUpBHPplt/hmbpGZpWwZm4FZB9GV\nUurIfQEV2g94QtV+eJcu6cWF/9wUtcqFzZ2wLo/J25uMYmqMo39irGSWR6RaFsUb\n7PVsVQ/WWDWyI96zvOSVI/Gqoqdz5OwSOR2xi6qDIywC6+oRfXu32rHOrEDCklJ+\nhdJ9jAOJ9g1RArtLu2+eCRlysaPdN4CxOmodb48wixJKq0hjyvUZHlIYTThUtQcO\nvWMpu7TOJ8nNnQlxRB70RzECOrFFd3MXoCVm/gV9BOsziEyv3wg6WuRMqBka5upC\nDvB3/9d0Q4VOYGPCY6PCaZC7nU/gemZQR3+HkMmfv3eKxcw3Gy7wHuGXvo3x3lX4\n1GYgxoWhxSIYeGkmF3qb3DhTgXwtODLa8PtSj3M6T+UPeyp/0jvYk0MPgrcI96/o\nCBJHb+7taeWwOWtURN1U\n=sd6l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T13:35:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received