.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/decentraland/sites/commit/5ad83d1f3871f31feafc43806be1c33d47931fcc","node_id":"C_kwDOQVSgz9oAKDVhZDgzZDFmMzg3MWYzMWZlYWZjNDM4MDZiZTFjMzNkNDc5MzFmY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/decentraland/sites/commit/df023df022146b6386a69009321da754981ecf5f","sha":"df023df022146b6386a69009321da754981ecf5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/commits/df023df022146b6386a69009321da754981ecf5f"}],"sha":"5ad83d1f3871f31feafc43806be1c33d47931fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/commits/5ad83d1f3871f31feafc43806be1c33d47931fcc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1120791?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/LautaroPetaccio","id":1120791,"login":"LautaroPetaccio","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjA3OTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/commits/df023df022146b6386a69009321da754981ecf5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:43:48Z","email":"1120791+LautaroPetaccio@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Lautaro Petaccio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:43:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: deploy through the cdn-deploy action only (#565)\n\n* chore: add example workflow for cdn-deploy integration\n\nshows how @dcl/sites would adopt decentraland/actions/cdn-deploy in place\nof the current oddish + static-sites-pipeline + set-rollout relay, in a\nsingle in-job step that uploads to s3 via github oidc and patches the\ncloudflare kv inline.\n\nthe file is inert: every job is gated on the CDN_DEPLOY_EXAMPLE_ENABLED\nrepo variable (unset), so merging it does not deploy anything or interfere\nwith build-release.yml / set-rollout*.yml. it documents three paths:\n\n- push to master: build once, deploy dev (zone), repoint stg (today) at\n  the same bytes (one upload, kv-only for the second env)\n- release published: promote the stg build to prod under the release tag\n  WITHOUT rebuilding, via the redeploy s3-copy + kv repoint\n- manual dispatch: rollout/rollback by moving the kv pointer (repoint)\n\n* chore: pin actions to commit shas and run every job on node 24\n\n- actions/checkout -> df4cb1c # v6.0.3\n- actions/setup-node -> 48b55a0 # v6.4.0\n- add a node 24 setup step to the promote-prod and repoint jobs so the\n  action runs under node 24 even though they do no checkout/build\n\n* chore: use the cdn-deploy reusable workflow in the example\n\nswitch the example from calling the cdn-deploy composite action directly\nto the reusable workflow decentraland/actions/.github/workflows/cdn-deploy.yml,\nso each path is a small with:/secrets: block:\n\n- push -> deploy-dev (build once, zone) then deploy-stg (repoint today at\n  the same version via the reusable workflow''s `version` output)\n- release -> promote-prod (redeploy: copy stg build to the tag, point org)\n- workflow_dispatch -> repoint\n\nstill inert (gated on CDN_DEPLOY_EXAMPLE_ENABLED).\n\n* chore: slim the example to the state-aware reusable workflow\n\n- secrets: inherit (org CF_KV_API_TOKEN / ROLLOUTS_SLACK_WEBHOOK); account id,\n  role and KV namespaces come from org vars + action defaults, so the jobs\n  carry almost no config\n- dev-stg derives package-name/deployment-path from package.json and repoints\n  zone+today from one upload\n- release stages the build under the tag (deployment-environments ''[]'', no KV);\n  manual dispatch switches a chosen env''s KV\n\n* chore: manual-deploy job takes a version or a commit\n\nthe workflow_dispatch job now deploys a chosen environment + a build picked\nby version OR commit (e.g. promote dev''s build to stg by its commit), on top\nof the automatic push/release flow.\n\n* chore: list the CF_NS_* org secrets in the example setup notes\n\nthe KV namespace ids moved out of the action into org secrets, so the\none-time org setup now includes CF_NS_ZONE / CF_NS_TODAY / CF_NS_ORG.\n\n* chore: correct stage-release comment (reusable workflow now always checks out)\n\nthe reusable workflow checks out the release commit, so the copy source is\nderived from the repo-root package.json; package-name is optional.\n\n* chore: use the cdn-deploy action directly (build in the job, pass dist-path)\n\ndrop the reusable-workflow indirection: each job checks out + builds (or\nchecks out for the base version) and calls decentraland/actions/cdn-deploy\nwith dist-path, wiring the org secrets/vars and a per-repo concurrency group.\nthe UI owns its build artifact.\n\n* chore: bring the cdn-deploy example up to the broker-based action\n\nThe example still passed `aws-role-to-assume` and five `cloudflare-*` inputs.\nNone of them exist any more: the action holds no Cloudflare token and no IAM\nrole, and authenticates to the cdn-deploy broker with a GitHub OIDC token\ninstead. As written, the jobs also could not have worked:\n\n- the push job repointed `today`, which now needs the job to declare a\n  matching GitHub environment AND a release version, so a commit build from\n  master was refused twice over;\n- the release job set a `version` with nothing to fill it from, so it staged\n  nothing at all — `copy-from-commit` is what makes the broker copy the\n  tagged commit''s build, and it is opt-in so that a merely-absent version\n  fails rather than being filled with whatever this commit built;\n- the manual job offered an environment choice without declaring\n  `environment:` on the job, so no environment claim was ever issued and\n  today/org were refused.\n\nRewritten as the three jobs the broker''s rules actually describe: push\npublishes a commit build to zone, a release stages the tag, and a manual\npromotion names a released version for today or org from a job that declares\nthe environment. Rolling back is that same promotion with an older version.\n\nThe adoption notes no longer ask for org-wide Cloudflare secrets, which were\nthe thing this replaces. They ask for the two environment settings that are\nnow the whole control: required reviewers, and \"Protected branches only\" —\nGitHub auto-creates a missing environment with neither, and the broker cannot\ntell that apart from an approved one.\n\n* chore: drop the slack webhook, and let today take a commit build\n\nThe broker announces rollouts itself now, so the webhook is no longer an\ninput and no longer a secret this repo needs. With it gone the example uses\nno secrets at all: `permissions: { id-token: write }` is the whole of it.\n\nAlso corrects the environment rules. Only org requires a release; today takes\na commit build, which is the point of staging — it is where a candidate is\nlooked at before anyone cuts a release.\n\n* chore: deploy through the cdn-deploy action only\n\nReplaces the three-workflow relay with one workflow. build-release.yml\npublished @dcl/sites to npm so a GitLab job could mirror it to the CDN, and\nset-rollout.yml then reacted to that job''s deployment_status; set-rollout-manual.yml\nwas the manual promotion. All three are the relay the action replaces, and\nleaving any of them in place would mean two pipelines writing the same S3\nprefixes and the same KV records.\n\nCarried over from build-release.yml deliberately: SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN on the\nbuild step, so @sentry/vite-plugin keeps uploading source maps, and HUSKY=0\non the install. What is NOT carried over is the npm publish itself — that\nexisted to get the bytes to the CDN, which is now done directly.\n\nThe workflow is live rather than gated behind CDN_DEPLOY_EXAMPLE_ENABLED:\nwith the old ones deleted, a gated one would mean the site never deploys at\nall. It must not merge before the broker is live in prd.\n\nCLAUDE.md described the relay as how production is built; it now describes\nthis.\n\n* fix: set the deployed version before building, as oddish used to\n\nscripts/prebuild.cjs derives two things from package.json''s version:\nREACT_APP_WEBSITE_VERSION, which becomes the Sentry release name, and\nVITE_BASE_URL, which is the CDN path every built asset is requested from.\n\nThe old workflow ran oddish-action with only-update-versions before building,\nwhich rewrote that version to the deterministic snapshot. Dropping oddish\nwithout replacing that step left package.json at its committed value, so the\nbuild would have baked in\n\n  https://cdn.decentraland.org/@dcl/sites/0.0.1\n\nwhile the action uploaded the bytes to\n\n  https://cdn.decentraland.org/@dcl/sites/0.0.1-commit-<sha7>\n\nEvery asset would 404. The Sentry side is the same root cause and quieter:\nevery commit build would have uploaded source maps to one release named after\nthe committed version, overwriting each other and never matching the bundle\nactually running.\n\nThe version is now computed once, written to package.json before the build,\nand passed back to the action explicitly so it does not suffix an\nalready-suffixed base.\n\n* fix: rebuild a release under its own version instead of copying\n\nA release has to serve everything from /1.2.3/ — that is what distinguishes\nit from the pre-release at /1.2.3-commit-<sha7>/. It cannot be a copy of the\ncommit build, because prebuild bakes VITE_BASE_URL into the bundle from\npackage.json''s version: those bytes ask for their assets from the commit\npath, whatever prefix they are copied into.\n\nSo the release event now checks out the tag, sets the version to it, builds,\nand uploads that. The Sentry release comes out as sites@1.2.3 for the same\nreason, which is what a release should be named.\n\nThis is not specific to this repo. builder, auth and wearable-preview all\nderive the CDN url from package.json''s version the same way, so a server-side\ncopy cannot produce a correct release for any of them.\n\n* chore: keep set-rollout-manual.yml until the broker has something to publish\n\nThe broker refuses to publish a version without a completion marker, and\n`.deploy-complete.json` is introduced by this migration — so no version\ncurrently in the CDN bucket has one. On merge, @dcl/sites would have had no\npublishable version for org at all until one was staged through the new path,\nwith no way back.\n\nSo the manual rollout stays as a bridge, with a header saying what it is and\nwhen to delete it. It still goes the old way, set-rollout-action ->\nwebhooks-receiver -> KV, which is the path being replaced; that is the point\nof removing it once there is something to fall back to.\n\nSeeding markers for the live versions was the alternative and is worse than\nit looks: legacy oddish versions are shaped `0.67.1-<run>.commit-<sha>`, with\na dot rather than a hyphen before `commit`, so isCommitBuild reads them as\nreleases. A bucket-wide backfill would quietly let commit builds through the\norg gate.\n\nAlso corrects the promote job''s comment. Naming an older version is not a\nrollback on its own: records sort descending and the worker serves the first\nabove zero percent, so the newer build keeps serving everyone while the job\nreports success.\n\n* test: run the CDN deploy against the action branch\n\nTwo changes, both temporary and both marked in the file.\n\nThe action does not exist on decentraland/actions@main yet -- it is still on\nfeat/cdn-deploy-action, under review -- so every `uses:` points at that branch.\nTesting before the action merges is the whole point of this branch.\n\nAnd the workflow only triggered on a push to master, so nothing here could run\nit. workflow_dispatch cannot stand in: GitHub only offers it for workflows that\nalready exist on the default branch. So this branch joins the push trigger.\n\nBoth revert before merging. The action ref should end up a tag rather than a\nbranch or @main, since every other action in this file is pinned to a SHA.\n\n* test: let the action own the version and the build\n\nThe first end-to-end run deployed 1460 objects, wrote the rollout and reported\nsuccess while changing nothing: package.json says 0.0.1, so the commit version\nsorted 367th of 368 records and the worker kept serving 0.69.0.\n\nThe version is the action''s to resolve now -- anchored on the newest GitHub\nrelease rather than on a package.json nobody has updated in 69 minor versions\n-- and the build runs inside the action, between resolving and uploading, so\nthe version the assets are built for and the prefix they land in cannot drift.\nThat collapses all three jobs to a single `uses:`.\n\nSENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN moves to job level because a composite action''s steps do not\ninherit `env:` from the step that calls it.\n\n* test: re-run the CDN deploy against the fixed action\n\n* test: correct the promote job''s help text, and stop wrapping percentage\n\nThe dispatch form is the one place a human types a version by hand, and its\nhelp gave an example of a format the action stopped producing: versions carry a\nrun id now, `1.4.1-<runId>.commit-<sha7>`. Someone following it would enter a\nversion that does not exist in S3.\n\n`fromJSON` around the percentage is removed. The action validates it as an\ninteger in 0..100 and says so when it is not; `fromJSON` fails first, as a\nworkflow expression error, with nothing useful in it.\n\nNo other change is needed for the trimmed action surface: all three jobs\nalready pass only inputs that survive.\n\n* test: re-run the deploy against the fixed action\n\n* chore: pin the deploy to cdn-deploy-v1 and stop deploying from this branch\n\nBoth temporary changes from the end-to-end test are reverted now that\ndecentraland/actions has cut cdn-deploy-v1.0.0.\n\nThe three `uses:` are pinned to `@cdn-deploy-v1`, the floating major tag the\naction''s release workflow moves only onto a commit whose committed bundle\nmatches its sources -- it re-runs the tests and rebuilds before blessing one.\nThat was the last unpinned ref in this file; everything else is a commit SHA.\n\nAnd `ci/cdn-deploy-example` is out of the push trigger, so this branch stops\ndeploying to zone on every push. It was there because workflow_dispatch could\nnot stand in: GitHub only offers dispatch for workflows that already exist on\nthe default branch, so without it nothing here could run at all before merging.\nOnce this lands on master the push trigger covers it.","tree":{"sha":"ef2c090f7dc7e96eeb23f10418be26c1b1be6556","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/git/trees/ef2c090f7dc7e96eeb23f10418be26c1b1be6556"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/git/commits/df023df022146b6386a69009321da754981ecf5f","verification":{"payload":"tree ef2c090f7dc7e96eeb23f10418be26c1b1be6556\nparent ebbf0f4f6d64641062163c5aebe409cd9d3bc638\nauthor Lautaro Petaccio <1120791+LautaroPetaccio@users.noreply.github.com> 1790768628 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790768628 -0300\n\nchore: deploy through the cdn-deploy action only (#565)\n\n* chore: add example workflow for cdn-deploy integration\n\nshows how @dcl/sites would adopt decentraland/actions/cdn-deploy in place\nof the current oddish + static-sites-pipeline + set-rollout relay, in a\nsingle in-job step that uploads to s3 via github oidc and patches the\ncloudflare kv inline.\n\nthe file is inert: every job is gated on the CDN_DEPLOY_EXAMPLE_ENABLED\nrepo variable (unset), so merging it does not deploy anything or interfere\nwith build-release.yml / set-rollout*.yml. it documents three paths:\n\n- push to master: build once, deploy dev (zone), repoint stg (today) at\n  the same bytes (one upload, kv-only for the second env)\n- release published: promote the stg build to prod under the release tag\n  WITHOUT rebuilding, via the redeploy s3-copy + kv repoint\n- manual dispatch: rollout/rollback by moving the kv pointer (repoint)\n\n* chore: pin actions to commit shas and run every job on node 24\n\n- actions/checkout -> df4cb1c # v6.0.3\n- actions/setup-node -> 48b55a0 # v6.4.0\n- add a node 24 setup step to the promote-prod and repoint jobs so the\n  action runs under node 24 even though they do no checkout/build\n\n* chore: use the cdn-deploy reusable workflow in the example\n\nswitch the example from calling the cdn-deploy composite action directly\nto the reusable workflow decentraland/actions/.github/workflows/cdn-deploy.yml,\nso each path is a small with:/secrets: block:\n\n- push -> deploy-dev (build once, zone) then deploy-stg (repoint today at\n  the same version via the reusable workflow''s `version` output)\n- release -> promote-prod (redeploy: copy stg build to the tag, point org)\n- workflow_dispatch -> repoint\n\nstill inert (gated on CDN_DEPLOY_EXAMPLE_ENABLED).\n\n* chore: slim the example to the state-aware reusable workflow\n\n- secrets: inherit (org CF_KV_API_TOKEN / ROLLOUTS_SLACK_WEBHOOK); account id,\n  role and KV namespaces come from org vars + action defaults, so the jobs\n  carry almost no config\n- dev-stg derives package-name/deployment-path from package.json and repoints\n  zone+today from one upload\n- release stages the build under the tag (deployment-environments ''[]'', no KV);\n  manual dispatch switches a chosen env''s KV\n\n* chore: manual-deploy job takes a version or a commit\n\nthe workflow_dispatch job now deploys a chosen environment + a build picked\nby version OR commit (e.g. promote dev''s build to stg by its commit), on top\nof the automatic push/release flow.\n\n* chore: list the CF_NS_* org secrets in the example setup notes\n\nthe KV namespace ids moved out of the action into org secrets, so the\none-time org setup now includes CF_NS_ZONE / CF_NS_TODAY / CF_NS_ORG.\n\n* chore: correct stage-release comment (reusable workflow now always checks out)\n\nthe reusable workflow checks out the release commit, so the copy source is\nderived from the repo-root package.json; package-name is optional.\n\n* chore: use the cdn-deploy action directly (build in the job, pass dist-path)\n\ndrop the reusable-workflow indirection: each job checks out + builds (or\nchecks out for the base version) and calls decentraland/actions/cdn-deploy\nwith dist-path, wiring the org secrets/vars and a per-repo concurrency group.\nthe UI owns its build artifact.\n\n* chore: bring the cdn-deploy example up to the broker-based action\n\nThe example still passed `aws-role-to-assume` and five `cloudflare-*` inputs.\nNone of them exist any more: the action holds no Cloudflare token and no IAM\nrole, and authenticates to the cdn-deploy broker with a GitHub OIDC token\ninstead. As written, the jobs also could not have worked:\n\n- the push job repointed `today`, which now needs the job to declare a\n  matching GitHub environment AND a release version, so a commit build from\n  master was refused twice over;\n- the release job set a `version` with nothing to fill it from, so it staged\n  nothing at all — `copy-from-commit` is what makes the broker copy the\n  tagged commit''s build, and it is opt-in so that a merely-absent version\n  fails rather than being filled with whatever this commit built;\n- the manual job offered an environment choice without declaring\n  `environment:` on the job, so no environment claim was ever issued and\n  today/org were refused.\n\nRewritten as the three jobs the broker''s rules actually describe: push\npublishes a commit build to zone, a release stages the tag, and a manual\npromotion names a released version for today or org from a job that declares\nthe environment. Rolling back is that same promotion with an older version.\n\nThe adoption notes no longer ask for org-wide Cloudflare secrets, which were\nthe thing this replaces. They ask for the two environment settings that are\nnow the whole control: required reviewers, and \"Protected branches only\" —\nGitHub auto-creates a missing environment with neither, and the broker cannot\ntell that apart from an approved one.\n\n* chore: drop the slack webhook, and let today take a commit build\n\nThe broker announces rollouts itself now, so the webhook is no longer an\ninput and no longer a secret this repo needs. With it gone the example uses\nno secrets at all: `permissions: { id-token: write }` is the whole of it.\n\nAlso corrects the environment rules. Only org requires a release; today takes\na commit build, which is the point of staging — it is where a candidate is\nlooked at before anyone cuts a release.\n\n* chore: deploy through the cdn-deploy action only\n\nReplaces the three-workflow relay with one workflow. build-release.yml\npublished @dcl/sites to npm so a GitLab job could mirror it to the CDN, and\nset-rollout.yml then reacted to that job''s deployment_status; set-rollout-manual.yml\nwas the manual promotion. All three are the relay the action replaces, and\nleaving any of them in place would mean two pipelines writing the same S3\nprefixes and the same KV records.\n\nCarried over from build-release.yml deliberately: SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN on the\nbuild step, so @sentry/vite-plugin keeps uploading source maps, and HUSKY=0\non the install. What is NOT carried over is the npm publish itself — that\nexisted to get the bytes to the CDN, which is now done directly.\n\nThe workflow is live rather than gated behind CDN_DEPLOY_EXAMPLE_ENABLED:\nwith the old ones deleted, a gated one would mean the site never deploys at\nall. It must not merge before the broker is live in prd.\n\nCLAUDE.md described the relay as how production is built; it now describes\nthis.\n\n* fix: set the deployed version before building, as oddish used to\n\nscripts/prebuild.cjs derives two things from package.json''s version:\nREACT_APP_WEBSITE_VERSION, which becomes the Sentry release name, and\nVITE_BASE_URL, which is the CDN path every built asset is requested from.\n\nThe old workflow ran oddish-action with only-update-versions before building,\nwhich rewrote that version to the deterministic snapshot. Dropping oddish\nwithout replacing that step left package.json at its committed value, so the\nbuild would have baked in\n\n  https://cdn.decentraland.org/@dcl/sites/0.0.1\n\nwhile the action uploaded the bytes to\n\n  https://cdn.decentraland.org/@dcl/sites/0.0.1-commit-<sha7>\n\nEvery asset would 404. The Sentry side is the same root cause and quieter:\nevery commit build would have uploaded source maps to one release named after\nthe committed version, overwriting each other and never matching the bundle\nactually running.\n\nThe version is now computed once, written to package.json before the build,\nand passed back to the action explicitly so it does not suffix an\nalready-suffixed base.\n\n* fix: rebuild a release under its own version instead of copying\n\nA release has to serve everything from /1.2.3/ — that is what distinguishes\nit from the pre-release at /1.2.3-commit-<sha7>/. It cannot be a copy of the\ncommit build, because prebuild bakes VITE_BASE_URL into the bundle from\npackage.json''s version: those bytes ask for their assets from the commit\npath, whatever prefix they are copied into.\n\nSo the release event now checks out the tag, sets the version to it, builds,\nand uploads that. The Sentry release comes out as sites@1.2.3 for the same\nreason, which is what a release should be named.\n\nThis is not specific to this repo. builder, auth and wearable-preview all\nderive the CDN url from package.json''s version the same way, so a server-side\ncopy cannot produce a correct release for any of them.\n\n* chore: keep set-rollout-manual.yml until the broker has something to publish\n\nThe broker refuses to publish a version without a completion marker, and\n`.deploy-complete.json` is introduced by this migration — so no version\ncurrently in the CDN bucket has one. On merge, @dcl/sites would have had no\npublishable version for org at all until one was staged through the new path,\nwith no way back.\n\nSo the manual rollout stays as a bridge, with a header saying what it is and\nwhen to delete it. It still goes the old way, set-rollout-action ->\nwebhooks-receiver -> KV, which is the path being replaced; that is the point\nof removing it once there is something to fall back to.\n\nSeeding markers for the live versions was the alternative and is worse than\nit looks: legacy oddish versions are shaped `0.67.1-<run>.commit-<sha>`, with\na dot rather than a hyphen before `commit`, so isCommitBuild reads them as\nreleases. A bucket-wide backfill would quietly let commit builds through the\norg gate.\n\nAlso corrects the promote job''s comment. Naming an older version is not a\nrollback on its own: records sort descending and the worker serves the first\nabove zero percent, so the newer build keeps serving everyone while the job\nreports success.\n\n* test: run the CDN deploy against the action branch\n\nTwo changes, both temporary and both marked in the file.\n\nThe action does not exist on decentraland/actions@main yet -- it is still on\nfeat/cdn-deploy-action, under review -- so every `uses:` points at that branch.\nTesting before the action merges is the whole point of this branch.\n\nAnd the workflow only triggered on a push to master, so nothing here could run\nit. workflow_dispatch cannot stand in: GitHub only offers it for workflows that\nalready exist on the default branch. So this branch joins the push trigger.\n\nBoth revert before merging. The action ref should end up a tag rather than a\nbranch or @main, since every other action in this file is pinned to a SHA.\n\n* test: let the action own the version and the build\n\nThe first end-to-end run deployed 1460 objects, wrote the rollout and reported\nsuccess while changing nothing: package.json says 0.0.1, so the commit version\nsorted 367th of 368 records and the worker kept serving 0.69.0.\n\nThe version is the action''s to resolve now -- anchored on the newest GitHub\nrelease rather than on a package.json nobody has updated in 69 minor versions\n-- and the build runs inside the action, between resolving and uploading, so\nthe version the assets are built for and the prefix they land in cannot drift.\nThat collapses all three jobs to a single `uses:`.\n\nSENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN moves to job level because a composite action''s steps do not\ninherit `env:` from the step that calls it.\n\n* test: re-run the CDN deploy against the fixed action\n\n* test: correct the promote job''s help text, and stop wrapping percentage\n\nThe dispatch form is the one place a human types a version by hand, and its\nhelp gave an example of a format the action stopped producing: versions carry a\nrun id now, `1.4.1-<runId>.commit-<sha7>`. Someone following it would enter a\nversion that does not exist in S3.\n\n`fromJSON` around the percentage is removed. The action validates it as an\ninteger in 0..100 and says so when it is not; `fromJSON` fails first, as a\nworkflow expression error, with nothing useful in it.\n\nNo other change is needed for the trimmed action surface: all three jobs\nalready pass only inputs that survive.\n\n* test: re-run the deploy against the fixed action\n\n* chore: pin the deploy to cdn-deploy-v1 and stop deploying from this branch\n\nBoth temporary changes from the end-to-end test are reverted now that\ndecentraland/actions has cut cdn-deploy-v1.0.0.\n\nThe three `uses:` are pinned to `@cdn-deploy-v1`, the floating major tag the\naction''s release workflow moves only onto a commit whose committed bundle\nmatches its sources -- it re-runs the tests and rebuilds before blessing one.\nThat was the last unpinned ref in this file; everything else is a commit SHA.\n\nAnd `ci/cdn-deploy-example` is out of the push trigger, so this branch stops\ndeploying to zone on every push. It was there because workflow_dispatch could\nnot stand in: GitHub only offers dispatch for workflows that already exist on\nthe default branch, so without it nothing here could run at all before merging.\nOnce this lands on master the push trigger covers it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvPX0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATRcQAEB0ryLRXh8KiFGrmhW/QqRo\nwJBeov5tRhxi+LWYWE3q2EsJLs/0lXfi5UT2XijTYJdDmfQ+jCeiy9JhAx8hapE1\n4K4F8esJ7mzEMO1adB7R83Lq0ViTPQWYvh4wxgjrLxQ/hcgihygRvHUIxx5CuHJI\nky2kqN0gcM5Hr75z+LZ7SSQqhXfquIvycKxTGy3YeQlLacinVifhB/TDm6LQzS5F\nzKetE/b2Y7625IZGx7RLHJdUlhcxloab1FK3SVUZOz1AUnljBpZSwLXs0b47eY2v\nqFwfY4pvv8Yob/Wr55DZb8KLefQhzy/wYRMVPfPDTMVWwWxDPf/8PwavQaRYfsK7\njIxXM4iCdffSrwMhMqjSRgAnU87b0utj9gEe9KMwEytDAoCy7wlcuVrRhj30LKhw\nkExuJ/Aoz2AcK/auy0XA+qpkq60Fa46h9ydAFmBVwP0KDLqIoc0SRDD2zkRNt