:"https://github.com/kuruk-mm","id":12563266,"login":"kuruk-mm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNTYzMjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuruk-mm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuruk-mm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuruk-mm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuruk-mm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuruk-mm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kuruk-mm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/commits/15a823c5d7c796cb4a0e197df4cbb9020bf9831a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T13:18:04Z","email":"mateomiccino@gmail.com","name":"Mateo Miccino"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T13:18:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: serve the app-link association files for /jump (#861)\n\n* feat: serve the app-link association files for /jump\n\nThe explorer has always declared decentraland.org — applinks: in\nexport_presets.cfg, an autoVerify intent-filter in AndroidManifest.xml,\nand decentraland.org accepted as a host in lib/src/deep_link.rs — but the\nwebsite never served either .well-known file, so neither platform could\nverify the domain and every /jump link opened the browser instead.\n\nAdds both association files. iOS is scoped to /jump* and /mobile*; Android\nverifies the host, so its paths come from the app manifest and cannot be\nnarrowed from here.\n\nThe files reach the CDN bundle but not decentraland.org yet: the\nsites-deployer worker proxies only an allowlist of paths (robots.txt,\nwhitepaper*.pdf) and SPA-falls-back the rest. A companion MR there is\nrequired, same two-repo shape as the SEO PAGES map.\n\n* docs(jump): correct the router behaviour behind the iOS path scoping\n\nThe app''s router matches exact paths, so /places/place/:position and\n/jump/events?id= fall to the teleport default and silently no-op rather\nthan landing in Discover. Names godotengine as the manifest''s real home.","tree":{"sha":"d76669cc79145524ca74e2a64def4f0af6d7e84a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/git/trees/d76669cc79145524ca74e2a64def4f0af6d7e84a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/git/commits/15a823c5d7c796cb4a0e197df4cbb9020bf9831a","verification":{"payload":"tree d76669cc79145524ca74e2a64def4f0af6d7e84a\nparent d97521874ae158490032b3bb0c2cdd749720463f\nauthor Mateo Miccino <mateomiccino@gmail.com> 1790255884 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790255884 -0300\n\nfeat: serve the app-link association files for /jump (#861)\n\n* feat: serve the app-link association files for /jump\n\nThe explorer has always declared decentraland.org — applinks: in\nexport_presets.cfg, an autoVerify intent-filter in AndroidManifest.xml,\nand decentraland.org accepted as a host in lib/src/deep_link.rs — but the\nwebsite never served either .well-known file, so neither platform could\nverify the domain and every /jump link opened the browser instead.\n\nAdds both association files. iOS is scoped to /jump* and /mobile*; Android\nverifies the host, so its paths come from the app manifest and cannot be\nnarrowed from here.\n\nThe files reach the CDN bundle but not decentraland.org yet: the\nsites-deployer worker proxies only an allowlist of paths (robots.txt,\nwhitepaper*.pdf) and SPA-falls-back the rest. A companion MR there is\nrequired, same two-repo shape as the SEO PAGES map.\n\n* docs(jump): correct the router behaviour behind the iOS path scoping\n\nThe app''s router matches exact paths, so /places/place/:position and\n/jump/events?id= fall to the teleport default and silently no-op rather\nthan landing in Discover. Names godotengine as the manifest''s real home.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtSMMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEI0QAIjoW043BZK6KNaYG6SBfboU\neoegMvUojI6mien6FmHLUzttj5cg2AN49cU