rl":"https://github.com/LautaroPetaccio","id":1120791,"login":"LautaroPetaccio","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjA3OTE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LautaroPetaccio","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/commits/fb133c55fb365ddf4c8ec589d64c6614f079bdb9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T12:52:53Z","email":"1120791+LautaroPetaccio@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Lautaro Petaccio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T12:52:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): sign the ADR-44 payload that binds metadata casing (#777)\n\n* fix(auth): sign the ADR-44 payload that binds metadata casing\n\nThis app signs two requests that carry metadata, and both were emitting\nthe pre-6.0.0 payload:\n\n  sceneAdapter.ts   POST /get-scene-adapter to comms-gatekeeper, with\n                    {sceneId, parcel, realmName, signer}\n  accountDeletion   DELETE /accounts to auth-server, with {didToken}\n\nBoth carry uppercase, so folding them is lossy, and both services now\nverify the metadata bytes as delivered. They keep working today only\nbecause each service declares a legacy fallback listing exactly the keys\nthis app happens to spell canonically. That is a compatibility window,\nnot a resting state, and this app is the reason it is still open.\n\ndecentraland-crypto-fetch is also promoted to a real dependency. It was\nnever declared here and resolved transitively through\n@dcl/social-rpc-client, so the signer this app''s own code used was\nwhatever that package happened to pin -- a version nobody here chose, and\none that could change without any edit to this repository.\n\nFour packages move, and they have to move together:\n\n  decentraland-crypto-fetch  added at ^3.0.0\n  @dcl/hooks                 1.x declares crypto-fetch ^2.0.1 as a peer\n                             and cannot coexist with the 3.x signer\n  decentraland-ui2           3.22.0 pinned hooks to ^1.2.1, so hooks 2\n                             was unreachable until 3.22.1 widened it\n  @dcl/social-rpc-client     2.0.0 depended on crypto-fetch ^2.0.1, which\n                             left a second, nested copy of the old signer\n                             in the tree; 2.0.1 depends on ^3.0.0\n\nWithout the first three, adding the dependency fails at install with\nERESOLVE. Without the fourth it installs, but this app ships two signers\nemitting different payload formats depending on which code path runs.\n\nThe tree now holds exactly one decentraland-crypto-fetch, at 3.0.0.\n\nThe lockfile needed the stale @dcl/social-rpc-client entry dropped before\nnpm would re-resolve it: `^2.0.0` still admits the 2.0.0 recorded there,\nso npm kept it and the nested signer survived the bump. Widening a range\ndoes not by itself move a dependency a lockfile has already pinned.\n\n377 suites and 4360 tests pass. `tsc -b`, `npm ci` and eslint are clean.\n\n* fix: raise the node engine floor to match the resolved dependencies\n\nThe auth dependencies this branch pulls in (@dcl/crypto 3.7.0,\n@dcl/social-rpc-client 2.0.1 and decentraland-crypto-fetch 3.0.0) all\ndeclare `node >=22.0.0`, so the `^20.19.0` branch of the root engines\nrange advertised an install path none of them support.\n\nThe lowest floor that actually satisfies the whole tree is 22.12.0, not\n22.0.0: rolldown -- pulled in non-optionally by vite and\n@vitejs/plugin-react -- declares `^20.19.0 || >=22.12.0`, which is where\nthe previous range came from. Node 20.19 satisfies rolldown but not the\nauth packages, and Node 22.0-22.11 satisfies the auth packages but not\nrolldown, so the intersection of the two is `>=22.12.0`.\n\nVerified with `npm ci --engine-strict`, which now installs clean. CI\nalready runs Node 24.x.","tree":{"sha":"5f0dd1ca3008ee10beca9cbcfa71d62f6eb5d791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/git/trees/5f0dd1ca3008ee10beca9cbcfa71d62f6eb5d791"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/decentraland/sites/git/commits/fb133c55fb365ddf4c8ec589d64c6614f079bdb9","verification":{"payload":"tree 5f0dd1ca3008ee10beca9cbcfa71d62f6eb5d791\nparent eb7c6b7d43df6c06935e45d309aa6affcab5ca2c\nauthor Lautaro Petaccio <1120791+LautaroPetaccio@users.noreply.github.com> 1787835173 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787835173 -0300\n\nfix(auth): sign the ADR-44 payload that binds metadata casing (#777)\n\n* fix(auth): sign the ADR-44 payload that binds metadata casing\n\nThis app signs two requests that carry metadata, and both were emitting\nthe pre-6.0.0 payload:\n\n  sceneAdapter.ts   POST /get-scene-adapter to comms-gatekeeper, with\n                    {sceneId, parcel, realmName, signer}\n  accountDeletion   DELETE /accounts to auth-server, with {didToken}\n\nBoth carry uppercase, so folding them is lossy, and both services now\nverify the metadata bytes as delivered. They keep working today only\nbecause each service declares a legacy fallback listing exactly the keys\nthis app happens to spell canonically. That is a compatibility window,\nnot a resting state, and this app is the reason it is still open.\n\ndecentraland-crypto-fetch is also promoted to a real dependency. It was\nnever declared here and resolved transitively through\n@dcl/social-rpc-client, so the signer this app''s own code used was\nwhatever that package happened to pin -- a version nobody here chose, and\none that could change without any edit to this repository.\n\nFour packages move, and they have to move together:\n\n  decentraland-crypto-fetch  added at ^3.0.0\n  @dcl/hooks                 1.x declares crypto-fetch ^2.0.1 as a peer\n                             and cannot coexist with the 3.x signer\n  decentraland-ui2           3.22.0 pinned hooks to ^1.2.1, so hooks 2\n                             was unreachable until 3.22.1 widened it\n  @dcl/social-rpc-client     2.0.0 depended on crypto-fetch ^2.0.1, which\n                             left a second, nested copy of the old signer\n                             in the tree; 2.0.1 depends on ^3.0.0\n\nWithout the first three, adding the dependency fails at install with\nERESOLVE. Without the fourth it installs, but this app ships two signers\nemitting different payload formats depending on which code path runs.\n\nThe tree now holds exactly one decentraland-crypto-fetch, at 3.0.0.\n\nThe lockfile needed the stale @dcl/social-rpc-client entry dropped before\nnpm would re-resolve it: `^2.0.0` still admits the 2.0.0 recorded there,\nso npm kept it and the nested signer survived the bump. Widening a range\ndoes not by itself move a dependency a lockfile has already pinned.\n\n377 suites and 4360 tests pass. `tsc -b`, `npm ci` and eslint are clean.\n\n* fix: raise the node engine floor to match the resolved dependencies\n\nThe auth dependencies this branch pulls in (@dcl/crypto 3.7.0,\n@dcl/social-rpc-client 2.0.1 and decentraland-crypto-fetch 3.0.0) all\ndeclare `node >=22.0.0`, so the `^20.19.0` branch of the root engines\nrange advertised an install path none of them support.\n\nThe lowest floor that actually satisfies the whole tree is 22.12.0, not\n22.0.0: rolldown -- pulled in non-optionally by vite and\n@vitejs/plugin-react -- declares `^20.19.0 || >=22.12.0`, which is where\nthe previous range came from. Node 20.19 satisfies rolldown but not the\nauth packages, and Node 22.0-22.11 satisfies the auth packages but not\nrolldown, so the intersection of the two is `>=22.12.0`.\n\nVerified with `npm ci --engine-strict`, which now installs clean. CI\nalready runs Node 24.x.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkDMlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASKIQAH5S55Grl7fCAiuMMioX3DwN\nGPdo4eHUGnH4UPQ1qnePUiMmXA9cCQBqO6FNfm+r/OT3tR1MVrmB6WCHiHYrMnFW\nfmq08D6eY+WLtjLIt0H95zxDnjEZz9rLoQUSWISsLtEJlrxEH41PKz1TJsgQXKB3\nN/WXj7268p46632dsUJ9/x2MXlusU05ggmQ3vNIJpuGHHIU4Jy/3F5g4qTFekyDv\nQJXrflm+dyPyg+iW3aB/NvNeaV0FluBzCzCUtcXwzs8uIRoJxrldhlJnftH2nA9z\ncr/Y1+HHBMWVJ85HKwrMyeZoBcyaAYlw8XRBEc8zcA5t5AAHllAX09YlK+HStUHW\n5eQ136ahjNCkdAPpwNC2gTfWbQMYbj1H3kmiHnY933uzWRmzgoIT9sd6TY1WICbp\nN2H5vG2o8HAvRJYN0uEFPRAO/xlspDKXbD+khuZEfSsBuf+w2SucL9CEe3tCgYHH\nvf2GzzV2cqJ3L7hf0H/XN3hrlniekpZWF42Kfr/bBlt+10wR15nmRjfn74PcPKht\nvayJe/5ofr/KjjktZl7TRFTWYRPbD0JggpyVUe+On8GmWPcx8WEpW4cvFg5YC6Rr\nb1LSapdeMsPgxwlsGxFdQhsYTdW4mPUsG82fX0SHDgwENWifJYxzzOSWdmMM0tCV\nw+pHgQ2C/Ct0ceP88vBS\n=YolO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T12:52:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/decentraland/sites/commit/fb133c55fb365ddf4c8ec589d64c6614f079bdb9","node_id":"C_kwDOQVSgz9oAKGZiMTMzYzU1ZmIzNjVkZG